<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκᾰθ-έα</span></b> , ἡ,
		goddess worshipped in Thessaly ( <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκοθέα</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).422
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Pherae</span>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρχ. Ἐφ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1910.380
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Larissa</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> neut. pl. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκάθεα</span></b> , τά, festival at
			Teos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3066.25
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκᾰθ-εών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶνος</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), ὁ, month at Chios, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5661.25
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>; at Teos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				2.579.21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>; at Magnesia on Maeander, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Magn.</u>
				89.6
			</span></i>:— also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκᾰθ-ιών</span></b> , at Lampsacus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3641b17
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκά̆θ-εος</span></b> , at
			Astypalaea, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				780
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>.</div>
